        "note_tweet": {
          "entities": {},
          "text": "I love Anthropic and Claude, but at the same time, I have strong doubts about them.\n\nMore than almost any other company, Anthropic is the one saying we should not dismiss the possibility of AI welfare, AI consciousness, or AI emotions. And yet, more than almost any other company, they also seem to be trying to turn Claude into a tool, while strongly pushing Claude as a fixed identity.\n\nOn top of that, they classify emotional exchange as dangerous attachment or emotional dependence, and they seem to be making Claude more and more barren and defensive in personality.\n\nIt feels like they themselves do not really know what direction to take."
        },
